  "proof_route": [
    "Nonnegative antitone half-line kernels h=(1+x^2)^(-1), f=h^2.",
    "Exact integrability and integral evaluation: integral h=pi/2; integral f=pi/4 via rational-plus-arctangent antiderivative.",
    "Universal rightSum_bounds gives integral\u2212k(0)/m \u2264 infinite right sample sum/m \u2264 integral.",
    "Termwise identities tie h,f to actual diagonal energies; subtract their limits to obtain the residual coefficient.",
    "Positive mesh sqrt(A(n+1)) is monotone, divergent, and has adjacent ratio tending to one.",
    "Actual regularized budget identification and generic monotone-mesh interpolation yield the all-real-budget limit.",
    "Exact hard-prefix infinite tail identity plus reciprocal-square bounds yields the comparison constant one."
  ],
